  ],
  "heading": "\\lattice",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{lattice}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\lattice]\nDeclares: L ::= (X, R, meet(a_, b_), join(a_, b_)) is \\set via X\nspecifies:\n. R is \\partial.order:on{X}\n. meet(a_, b_) is \\function:on{X \\.set.cross./ X}:to{X}\n. join(a_, b_) is \\function:on{X \\.set.cross./ X}:to{X}\nsatisfies:\n. forAll: a, b \"in\" X\n  then:\n  . R(meet(a, b), a)\n  . R(meet(a, b), b)\n  . R(a, join(a, b))\n  . R(b, join(a, b))\n. forAll:\n  . a, b \"in\" X\n  . x \"in\" X\n  where:\n  . R(x, a)\n  . R(x, b)\n  then: R(x, meet(a, b))\n. forAll:\n  . a, b \"in\" X\n  . x \"in\" X\n  where:\n  . R(a, x)\n  . R(b, x)\n  then: R(join(a, b), x)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"lattice\"\n. description: \"A lattice is a partially ordered set in which each pair has a\n                greatest lower bound and a least upper bound.\"\nId: \"1454c69c-e96e-4c4e-98e4-7736db0ef0a7\"",
